---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/nav/SiteHeader.astro';
import DocPage from '../../components/docs/DocPage.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import { rustDark, rustLight } from '../../../shiki-rust-themes.mjs';
import {
  CARGO_ADD,
  CARGO_DEP,
  CRATE_VERSION,
  CRATE_RELEASED,
  CRATESIO_URL,
  DOCSRS_URL,
  MSRV,
  CRATE_URL,
  GITHUB_URL,
} from '../../consts';

const SHIKI = { light: rustLight, dark: rustDark };

const title = 'Add the crate — DeepCausality Quantum';
const description =
  'Install from crates.io, the feature flags, the no-std story, the workspace MSRV, and what the default build actually compiles.';

const add = CARGO_ADD;

const gitdep = `[dependencies]
${CARGO_DEP}`;

const dep = `[dependencies]
deep_causality_quantum = "${CRATE_VERSION}"`;

const qpu = `[dependencies]
deep_causality_quantum = { version = "${CRATE_VERSION}", features = ["qpu"] }`;

const nostd = `[dependencies]
deep_causality_quantum = { version = "${CRATE_VERSION}", default-features = false, features = ["no-std"] }`;

const run = `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/deepcausality-rs/deep_causality.git
cd deep_causality
cargo run --release -p quantum_examples --example qcm_freeze_check`;

const features = [
  {
    name: 'std',
    on: 'default',
    what: 'The standard-library build. Enables std on every workspace dependency the crate pulls in.',
  },
  {
    name: 'qcm',
    on: 'default',
    what: 'The causal-model slice: CausalStructure, the Markov freeze check, and the C₃-exclusion faithfulness check. It pulls in deep_causality for the causal graph, which is std-only, so qcm implies std and is off on a bare-metal build.',
  },
  {
    name: 'alloc',
    on: 'off',
    what: 'Allocation without the standard library. Implied by both std and no-std.',
  },
  {
    name: 'no-std',
    on: 'off',
    what: 'The bare-metal build. Implies alloc and switches every workspace dependency to its own no-std feature.',
  },
  {
    name: 'qpu',
    on: 'off',
    what: 'The emergent QPU seam: QpuSampler, ShotHistogram, the shots-to-Uncertain bridges, qpu_effect and the in-process SimQpu. Adds deep_causality_uncertain, and nothing network-facing or async.',
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/start/">
  <SiteHeader slot="header" />

  <DocPage
    eyebrow="Getting started"
    title="Add the crate"
    lede={`Version ${CRATE_VERSION}, MIT licensed, released on crates.io on ${CRATE_RELEASED}.`}
    sourceHref={CRATE_URL}
    sourceLabel="deep_causality_quantum"
  >
    <h2>The dependency</h2>

    <Code code={add} lang="bash" themes={SHIKI} />

    <p>Or by hand:</p>

    <Code code={dep} lang="toml" themes={SHIKI} />

    <p>
      The generated API reference is on
      <a href={DOCSRS_URL}>docs.rs</a>, built with all features enabled, and the
      release itself is on <a href={CRATESIO_URL}>crates.io</a>. To track work
      that has not been released yet, take the branch instead:
    </p>

    <Code code={gitdep} lang="toml" themes={SHIKI} />

    <p>
      The workspace minimum supported Rust version is {MSRV}, from
      <code>rust-version</code> in the root manifest. The crate opts into the
      workspace lints, which include <code>unsafe_code = "forbid"</code>; there
      is no unsafe code here and no exemption.
    </p>

    <h2>What the default build gives you</h2>

    <p>
      The default feature set is <code>["std", "qcm"]</code>. That compiles the
      operator layer, the gate kernels and their causal-monad wrappers, the
      verdict layer, and the causal-model slice with its freeze-time checks. It
      does not compile the QPU seam.
    </p>

    <p>
      No feature setting adds a network dependency or an async runtime. The
      external dependency list for this crate is empty; everything it uses is a
      workspace path dependency.
    </p>

    <h2>Feature flags</h2>

    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Feature</th>
            <th scope="col">Default</th>
            <th scope="col">What it turns on</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {features.map((f) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code class="fname">{f.name}</code></td>
              <td>
                {f.on === 'default'
                  ? <span class="status status-validated">on</span>
                  : <span class="status status-roadmap">off</span>}
              </td>
              <td class="fwhat">{f.what}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>The QPU seam</h3>

    <Code code={qpu} lang="toml" themes={SHIKI} />

    <h3>Bare metal</h3>

    <Code code={nostd} lang="toml" themes={SHIKI} />

    <p>
      A <code>no-std</code> build loses the causal-model slice, because
      <code>qcm</code> depends on the std-only causal graph. What remains is the
      operator layer, the gate kernels and the verdict layer, all of which use
      <code>alloc</code> and compile without the standard library.
    </p>

    <h2>Run something first</h2>

    <p>
      The fastest way to see whether the crate does what you need is the freeze
      check, which is the crate's reason for existing and runs in a few seconds
      after the workspace builds.
    </p>

    <Code code={run} lang="bash" themes={SHIKI} />

    <p>
      The <code>--depth 1</code> matters on an ordinary connection: the
      full-history pack is large, and the clone is the slow step. The example
      prints two runs, one that freezes and one that aborts naming the offending
      pair. The <a href="/examples/qcm-freeze-check/">example page</a> walks
      through the output line by line.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to go next</h2>

    <ul class="hairline-list">
      <li><a href="/qcm/">The model, the freeze check and faithfulness</a></li>
      <li><a href="/operators/">The operator layer the checks are built from</a></li>
      <li><a href="/formalization/">What is proved in LEAN, and what is not</a></li>
      <li><a href={DOCSRS_URL}>API reference on docs.rs ↗</a></li>
      <li><a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/issues`}>Open an issue ↗</a></li>
    </ul>
  </DocPage>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: var(--t-body-sm); }
  th, td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-1);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  th { color: var(--fg-0); font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
  tbody tr:hover { background: var(--bg-1); }
  .fname { font-size: var(--t-mono-sm); color: var(--fg-0); background: none; padding: 0; }
  .fwhat { color: var(--fg-1); max-width: 52ch; }
</style>
